```swift
func identifyVerbalIrony(sentence: String) -> String? {
    // Define a list of common ironic phrases and their explanations
    let ironicPhrases = [
        "I just love getting stuck in traffic": "Sarcasm - the speaker actually hates getting stuck in traffic",
        "What a beautiful day to stay indoors": "Sarcasm - the speaker actually wants to go outside",
        "Great, another meeting": "Dramatic irony - the speaker knows that the meeting will be bad but the other participants don't",
        "Thanks for the ticket, officer": "Verbal irony - the speaker is actually angry at the officer for giving them a ticket",
        "I'm so glad it's raining on my wedding day": "Situational irony - rain is usually considered bad luck on a wedding day",
        // Add more ironic phrases and their explanations here
    ]

    // Check if the sentence contains any of the ironic phrases
    for (phrase, explanation) in ironicPhrases {
        if sentence.lowercased().contains(phrase.lowercased()) {
            return explanation
        }
    }

    // If no ironic phrase is found, return nil
    return nil
}
```
This function defines a list of common ironic phrases and their explanations, then checks if the given sentence contains any of them (ignoring case sensitivity). If a match is found, the function returns the corresponding explanation. If no match is found, the function returns nil.
Here's an example usage of the function:
