One common application of the Jordan canonical form is in solving linear differential equations. By finding the Jordan canonical form of the coefficient matrix, we can easily write down the solution to the differential equation in terms of exponential functions and polynomials.
In MATLAB, we can use the `jordan` function to compute the Jordan canonical form of a matrix. Here's an example:
