```
public class CircularPathDisplacement {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double radius = 10; // radius of the circular path
        double pi = 3.14; // value of pi
        double displacement; // variable to store the displacement

        // table of values for velocity and time
        double[][] table = {{5, 10}, {3, 8}, {7, 5}};

        // loop through the table
        for (int i = 0; i < table.length; i++) {
            // calculate the displacement using the formula D = V x T x 2 x pi x R / T
            displacement = table[i][0] * table[i][1] * 2 * pi * radius / table[i][1];

            // print the displacement for each set of values in the table
            System.out.println("Displacement for Velocity " + table[i][0] + " m/s and Time " + table[i][1] + " s is " + displacement + " m");
        }
    }
}
```
In this code, we first define the radius of the circular path and the value of pi. Then, we define a variable to store the displacement. We also define a table of values for velocity and time.
Next, we loop through the table and calculate the displacement for each set of values using the formula D = V x T x 2 x pi x R / T. We then print the displacement for each set of values in the table.
Note that we multiply the velocity and time by 2 in the formula because the object travels half the circumference of the circle in the given time.

