<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Merge Sort Visualization</title>
    <style>
      body {
        font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      }
      .chart {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: row;
        justify-content: center;
        align-items: flex-end;
        height: 300px;
      }
      .bar {
        width: 20px;
        margin-right: 5px;
        background-color: blue;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>Merge Sort Visualization</h1>
    <label for="input">Enter an array of integers:</label>
    <input type="text" id="input" value="[5, 3, 8, 6, 2, 7, 1, 4]">
    <button onclick="sort()">Sort</button>
    <div class="chart" id="chart"></div>
    <script>
      function sort() {
        const input = document.getElementById('input').value;
        const arr = JSON.parse(input);
        const sortedArr = mergeSort(arr);
        drawChart(sortedArr);
      }
      function drawChart(arr) {
        const chart = document.getElementById('chart');
        chart.innerHTML = '';
        for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
          const bar = document.createElement('div');
          bar.classList.add('bar');
          bar.style.height = `${arr[i] * 20}px`;
          chart.appendChild(bar);
        }
      }
      function mergeSort(arr) {
        if (arr.length <= 1) {
          return arr;
        }
        const mid = Math.floor(arr.length / 2);
        const left = mergeSort(arr.slice(0, mid));
        const right = mergeSort(arr.slice(mid));
        return merge(left, right);
      }
      function merge(left, right) {
        let i = 0;
        let j = 0;
        const result = [];
        while (i < left.length && j < right.length) {
          if (left[i] < right[j]) {
            result.push(left[i]);
            i++;
          } else {
            result.push(right[j]);
            j++;
          }
        }
        return result.concat(left.slice(i)).concat(right.slice(j));
      }
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
```
When the user enters an array of integers and clicks the "Sort" button, the `sort()` function is called, which parses the input and calls the `mergeSort()` function to sort the array. The sorted array is then passed to the `drawChart()` function, which creates a series of divs with a class of "bar" and a height proportional to the value of the corresponding element in the array. These divs are appended to the "chart" div, which is a flex container that aligns the bars along the bottom edge. The result is a bar chart that shows the user how the merge sort algorithm works step by step.

